<article class="env-lemma" id="0128">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0128">Lemma <span data-tag="0128">12.19.14</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $A \to B \to C$ be a complex of filtered objects of $\mathcal{A}$. Assume $\alpha : A \to B$ and $\beta : B \to C$ are strict morphisms of filtered objects. Then $\text{gr}(\mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(\beta )/\mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(\alpha )) = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(\text{gr}(\beta ))/\mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(\text{gr}(\alpha )))$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows formally from Lemma <a href="/tag/05SP" data-tag="05SP">12.19.12</a> and the fact that $\mathop{\mathrm{Coim}}(\alpha ) \cong \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(\alpha )$ and $\mathop{\mathrm{Coim}}(\beta ) \cong \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(\beta )$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/05SI" data-tag="05SI">12.19.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>